w floor area, fine.\n\nMaybe create two-point-ish simple: back wall with window and shelf, lower cabinets straight on. Counter horizontal line at y=620, cabinets to y=855, floor starts 855. Full width. Then add foreground table at right? That could fill lower area. Maybe lower-left chair/cat.\n\nLet's frame:\n- Wall: x=0..1600, y=0..720, plaster warm ivory. Wall has subtle vignette, light patch.\n- Wainscot backsplash: y=520..640, zellige tiles in pale sage/cream painted.\n- Counter: x=80..1560, top surface y=618..650 (thickness 30), warm butcher block or cream stone; front base cabinets y=650..900; floor y=900..1000.\n- Window: x=150..600, y=90..500, with sky, hills, tree silhouettes, curtains. Deep recessed frame. Maybe arched top for coziness? Rectangular sash with transom.\n- Cabinet colors: muted olive/sage lower cabinets with beadboard panel, brass cup handles. Some upper open shelves on right above counter with plates, jars, trailing plant.\n- Right: stove/oven x=1150..1470, with kettle. Range hood? Perhaps omit, use shelf. Kettle on stovetop right.\n- Left: farmhouse sink under window? Counter under window, with faucet. Could draw sink basin and faucet at x=280..500.\n- Center: wooden cutting board, bread, cup, bowl, oranges, flowers.\n- Cat on counter? Sleeping cat on a stool near window or rug. Let's include a ginger cat curled on a chair at lower left, catching sun. But a cat on counter near sink might risk hygiene. Put a cushioned window seat? Window sill at y=500, cat sitting on sill silhouetted by morning sun—nice. Cat shape at right of window inner sill. Or a cat curled on a rug in sunbeam at lower left. That adds coziness. A cat on a chair is easier and good.\n\n- Hanging pendant light over center with warm glow.\n- A small round table in foreground left? But cat.\n\nMaybe do a wide farmhouse kitchen:\nLeft: window with curtain half-light, sink, plant, hanging mugs.\nCenter: counter with cutting board, bread, coffee, oranges, flowers.\nRight: stove with copper kettle, open shelving above.\nBottom left: wooden chair with cushion, cat sleeping.\nBottom right: woven runner rug? floor visible.\n\nSunbeams: translucent polygons from window at left to floor/counter at right, warm gradients. Add dust motes as small blurred circles.\n\nNeed textures: subtle wall plaster, wood grain, ceramic highlights, fabric weave.\n\nWe should build image with supersampling 2x maybe 3200x2000 then LANCZOS down to 1600x1000. Use PIL draw + custom functions for gradients, rounded rects, shadows, polygons, arcs, blur. Then add noise grain and soft light. Use ImageDraw at high res. Avoid too crowded.\n\nNeed maybe use numpy for gradients/noise. likely installed. Let's check."}
