20..370 y=660..840 with alpha 12, blur 10. This shows sunlight on cabinets, adds depth.\n\n- Add slight edge highlight on counter objects.\n\nLet's also add a small cat tail motion? no.\n\nComposition could use a small wall clock or hanging plant. Already shelf.\n\nThe right part above the range has empty wall? shelves fill. Good.\n\nMaybe the shelf jar arrangement is a bit toy-like; fine.\n\nOne issue: the leaves of the tree outside window are individually cut circles, but okay.\n\nA common critique: no true perspective, looks like a stage set. But still charming.\n\nMaybe could add a wooden stool at bottom left to give foreground depth. A small round stool with a cat? Cat already. Adding a stool that overlaps the lower cabinets and rug would give depth. Place at x=60..170 y=790..990, a three-legged stool, partially cropped, with a folded blanket. But it would cover the left cabinet and maybe flower vase; could be nice. Yet crowd.\n\nOr put a small wooden chair at lower left with a cushion and the cat? But cat on sill. no.\n\nCould place a basket on floor right of rug at x=820..920 y=880..990 with folded blanket. That fills empty floor between rug and range. But the floor is nice. Hmm.\n\nLet's focus on lighting and final quality.\n\nNeed maybe ensure no unnatural artifacts: the leaves from hanging plant extend down near range top? They end at 376, above range. Fine.\n- The mug handles under shelf: handles drawn to the right, at x+27; next mug x=1118, handle ends 1145, next mug body starts 1153, fine.\n- Flower vase: handle extends to x1+22=230, overlapping herb pot left edge 231. Visually in image, the vase handle might be hidden behind the herb pot? It's drawn before herb pot, so herb pot covers it. Indeed handle maybe not visible. Fine.\n- Flower stems look nice.\n\nWe might need to add a little contrast shadow between backsplash and counter. present.\n- The sink's white front is very large. Could add a subtle horizontal shadow under counter and upper rim. done.